T21:50:34Z"},{"number":803,"title":"Agent detection misses nix-wrapped Claude Code (.claude-unwrapped); devenv agents never appear in the agent panel","comments":19,"created_at":"2026-06-25T14:53:04Z"},{"number":2968,"title":"Keystrokes tear frames from TUIs that use synchronized output","comments":15,"created_at":"2026-08-19T04:04:04Z"},{"number":1178,"title":"Neovim colored underlines render incorrectly in Herdr compared with Kitty/tmux","comments":14,"created_at":"2026-07-08T09:24:30Z"},{"number":4649,"title":"Codex 0.157 shared daemon breaks per-pane sessions and HERDR_* env (waiting on upstream)","comments":12,"created_at":"2026-09-26T11:48:48Z"},{"number":3217,"title":"Running multiple agents simultaneously causes severe lag, high resource usage, and noisy fans on macOS after upgrading to v0.8.2","comments":11,"created_at":"2026-08-25T07:53:51Z"},{"number":3184,"title":"Prime Agent built-in herdr reporter: state reports work, session/identity don't (evidence + request)","comments":11,"created_at":"2026-08-24T11:24:54Z"},{"number":5272,"title":"0.9.4: labeled links no longer open in iTerm2 with mouse capture enabled","comments":10,"created_at":"2026-10-14T13:46:27Z"}],"discussions":[{"number":5997,"title":"Return to the previous workspace when a throwaway one closes","comments":0,"category":"Ideas","created_at":"2026-11-13T19:46:28Z"},{"number":5992,"title":"Reorder worktree children in the sidebar, and set env/cwd on `worktree open`","comments":0,"category":"Ideas","created_at":"2026-11-13T15:33:43Z"},{"number":5989,"title":"[idea]  Expose the TUI's current view (machine/workspace/pane) trhough cli for automation tasks","comments":0,"category":"Ideas","created_at":"2026-11-13T12:52:39Z"},{"number":5983,"title":"Herdr Tabs in centered alignment","comments":0,"category":"Ideas","created_at":"2026-11-13T04:16:36Z"},{"number":5978,"title":"Running many agents on one machine: GPU, memory and leftover processes","comments":0,"category":"Ideas","created_at":"2026-11-12T22:56:12Z"},{"number":5977,"title":"[idea] hc read: styled output (SGR) and cursor position, to tell an agent's ghost suggestion from a typed draft","comments":0,"category":"Ideas","created_at":"2026-11-12T22:39:04Z"},{"number":5974,"title":"[idea] Dock icon badge with the number of agents that need attention (macOS app)","comments":0,"category":"Ideas","created_at":"2026-11-12T20:55:47Z"},{"number":5971,"title":"Add custom titles for keybindings in the keybindings panel","comments":0,"category":"Ideas","created_at":"2026-11-12T16:21:58Z"}],"latest_release":{"name":"v0.9.5","tag":"v0.9.5","published_at":"2026-10-14T16:07:28Z","body":"This is a hotfix release for v0.9.4. See the v0.9.4 notes for the full feature release: https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr/releases/tag/v0.9.4\n\n### Fixed\n- Prefix shortcuts work again when the terminal sends the next key as plain text. This affected Tern, Chinese, Japanese and Korean input methods on macOS, and Ghostty `text:` keybinds that send the prefix and a key together. Workspace navigation had the same problem. (#5255)\n- Codex sessions no longer start with a \"clamping Interrupt hook timeout\" warning. Herdr no longer installs Codex turn hooks, and Codex status comes from screen detection again. Run `herdr integration install codex` to update. (#5246, #5278)\n- Claude Code questions show as blocked in named sessions. (#4573, #5192)\n- On Windows, plugin panes start even when a folder on `PATH` has the same name as the plugin's program. (#5267, #5269, thanks @JJLiebig)\n- On Windows, Claude Code session tracking works when the user folder name contains non-ASCII characters, such as Korean. (#5253, #5270, thanks @JJLiebig)\n- Adding a Windows machine no longer prints raw PowerShell progress output. (#4639, #5282, thanks @JJLiebig)\n","is_prerelease":false},"readme":true,"readme_zh":true,"news":[{"title":"Herdr: Agent multiplexer that lives in your terminal","url":"https://github.com/ogulcancelik/herdr","hn":"https://news.ycom